From fb9dbdc2d1831515011a1fbcec88de1f9413247f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:26:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] turn_session_activity: TUI update-pause reader uses
 the configured desktop.auto_continue bounds

The sidebar's `turn_live` reader counted a Desktop/TUI `core_update_pause` marker as live with
hard-coded bounds (enabled, 15 min, 2 attempts), while the producer (`_maybe_schedule_auto_continue`,
`_durable_continuation_due`) applies the configured `desktop.auto_continue.enabled`,
`freshness_minutes` and `max_attempts`. With auto-continue disabled or lowered, a pause that will never
continue read as a working turn for up to 15 minutes (PR #2545 review 5896585581, nit 1).

- `tui_gateway.turn_marker.auto_continue_bounds(config)`: the one parse of those bounds, same
  coercion as before (bool-ish enabled default true; freshness float minutes, floor 0; max_attempts int,
  negative/unparseable -> 2). `_auto_continue_config()` now delegates to it.
- `turn_session_activity._update_paused_tui_turns` reads each home's own config.yaml
  (`load_profile_config_effective`, lazily, only when a pause marker is present) and applies the
  same bounds, so a profile's sidebar row follows that profile's producer.
- The gateway 1 h bound comment now says what it is: the reader's own fail-closed cap, not a mirror
  of agent.gateway_auto_continue_freshness.
- Tests: `import json` moved to module top; new cases for disabled, freshness_minutes=5 with a
  10-min-old marker, exhausted max_attempts=1, a raised window, per-profile config, and the shared parse.

RED (fix reverted, tests kept): 6 new tests fail. GREEN: 26/26. Consumers (49 test files referencing
turn_marker / session_auto_continue / turn_session_activity / _auto_continue_config): 845 passed.
